Type: Package
Package: MeshUtils
Title: Utility Functions for 3D Meshes Based on 'CGAL'
Version: 0.0.1
Authors@R:
  c(person("Daniel", "Wollschlaeger", role=c("aut", "cre"), email="wollschlaeger@uni-mainz.de"),
    person("Stephane", "Laurent", role=c("aut")))
Maintainer: Daniel Wollschlaeger <wollschlaeger@uni-mainz.de>
Description: Basic processing of 3D meshes based on the 'C++'
    library 'CGAL' <https://www.cgal.org/>.
    Reads and writes common file formats for meshes and
    polygon soups.
    Supports mesh repair, remeshing, smoothing,
    subdivision ('Catmull-Clark', 'Doo-Sabin', 'Sqrt3', 'Loop'),
    Boolean operations (union, difference, intersection),
    surface reconstruction ('AFS', 'SSS', Poisson, alpha
    wrapping), (optimal) bounding box, and Hausdorff distance.
    Adapts code from packages 'Boov', 'PolygonSoup',
    and 'cgalMeshes' developed by Stephane Laurent.
License: GPL-3
URL: https://github.com/dwoll/MeshUtils/
BugReports: https://github.com/dwoll/MeshUtils/issues/
Depends:
    R (>= 4.0.0)
Imports:
    Rcpp (>= 1.0.9),
    rgl
LinkingTo:
    BH,
    Rcpp,
    RcppCGAL (>= 6.2.0),
    RcppEigen
Encoding: UTF-8
LazyData: true
SystemRequirements: C++17, gmp, mpfr
